# Code-reading notes on the Declaration node entry point

Start recording from the top of `lib/parser.js`. Declaration obtains the module binding on line 3, immediately followed by tokenizer, Comment, and AtRule:

```js
let Declaration = require('./declaration')
let tokenizer = require('./tokenize')
let Comment = require('./comment')
let AtRule = require('./at-rule')
```

This section only shows that the parser file has obtained these modules. Declaration is the node module entry point, and tokenizer is another binding; their adjacency does not mean that a token has already become a Declaration here. The file later also has bindings for Root and Rule, so treat the top as part of the parser's node-object setup for now, rather than inferring construction order from the names.

This pass only confirms the entry point. Continue reading by locating the first use of the Declaration binding within `lib/parser.js`, then return to `./declaration` to inspect the node itself. The `SAFE_COMMENT_NEIGHBOR` on line 10 is also within the top section, but its relationship to the comment near the declaration has not yet been recorded.
